      }
    ],
    "sources": [
      {
        "quote": "/isi/ → /isɨ/ → /isu/"
      },
      {
        "quote": "Originally 倚子 (ishi), referring to seats with or without rests used by higher court officials. With the arrival of Zen Buddhism to Japan, possibly a later borrowing from Middle Chinese 椅子 (MC 'jeX tsiX) or directly from Mandarin 椅子 (yǐzi, literally \"chair\" + diminutive suffix), the meaning shifted to wooden seats used by priests."
      }
    ],
